# Regenerable backcast dashboard bundles — do not track.
# Added by the repo clone-bloat audit, 2026-07-22
# (docs/handoffs/repo-clone-bloat-audit-2026-07.md). The Deploy-Pages workflow
# runs with permissions: contents:read and assembles these three files into the
# _site artifact from the committed registry/<id>.json + bench/ sidecars at
# deploy time (`scripts/build_manifest.py --site-dir _site`); it never commits
# them back to main. The tracked copies were pure derived-file churn
# (benchmark.js is ~0.6 MB, re-written on every dashboard change) and a
# concurrent-session merge hazard. A local file:// preview refreshes them with
# `python3 scripts/build_manifest.py`. This SUPERSEDES the now-stale "These ARE
# committed / the Deploy workflow is the single writer" note in the root
# .gitignore. The registry/, runs/<id>.js and bench/ keeper sidecars these are
# built FROM stay tracked — those are the committed deliverables.
manifest.js
benchmark.js
completeness.js
